2020 is the year of the Xbox series X  but Microsoft isn't forgetting about the  regular Xbox one just yet  the latest dashboard update for the  console has arrived for testers at least  and it's a big one  the Xbox one UI is notorious for being  difficult to use but this update  improves things update 2002 which makes  me wonder if there have been 2001  updates before this is now available for  people in the Xbox Insider alpha ring  and in this video we're covering five  new features that make the console look  and perform even better  starting off you will immediately notice  that the homescreen is now much more  streamlined the so-called twists at the  top of the screen have been removed with  those gone the screen is less cluttered  so you can see more of it at a glance  you'll notice new smaller tiles for your  most played games and apps and below  that you'll see spotlight advertisements  for things like mixer deals and more  with all the freed up space you wonder  if Microsoft will eventually fill it  with ads but time will tell  scrolling further down the page you'll  see new rows for game paths  store mixer and community along with  individual games further down the page  hovering over these you'll see a preview  of its contents at a glance for example  the game pastro shows you big tiles for  games recommended to you i have the  witcher 3 on my screen as well as taps  for recently added games the store page  meanwhile highlights the current deals  available along with other tabs for  things like new games top paid games  specials free games and more you can  customize what rows show up in your home  screen which is a nice option if you  don't want to be inundated by any  particular thing and as usual it bears  mentioning again here that you can  customize your background in colors as  well as the transparency levels of the  home panel and tiles those features  haven't gone away moving to the games  and apps UI you'll notice that the  grouping is improved it's now much  easier to navigate and see your games at  a glance yet you can tell I like sports  games and shooters there are also now  labels for trials and demos as you can  see here with plants vs. zombies battle  for neighbor Ville before this page  showed every game you owned or had  access to through Xbox Live Gold or game  paths and it was distracting and  overwhelming to see so much information  all at once now if you want to see your  full library you just click full library  given the increasing size of games these  days and the big patches that can make  them even bigger you're likely to need  to delete games in DLC often to free up  space the new update makes it easier by  showing you things like leftover add-ons  that you might have installed but never  used there is also a shrinkable games  tab that shows you games that can  decrease in file size while still being  played I don't have any of these but you  might  another new feature in the update is the  ability to view images and animated gifs  in messages on Xbox Live yes we're sure  nothing will go wrong here but also  don't worry in your privacy settings you  can select who is able to send you  messages another nice feature in the  Xbox one update is the ability to set  where notifications show up on your  screen there are six different locations  to choose from from across the screen  this is great because previously the  notifications could pop up in places  that would obscure the action on the  screen microsoft says your preferred  location will be the default but some  games may move the location to provide  the best user experience you can check  out the full blog post on Microsoft's  web site to see a rundown of everything  that's new in the update including  improvements a mixer and data storage  overall this new Xbox one dashboard is a  welcome improvement on what has  historically been a difficult to use  platform it still takes you more than a  few button presses to get where you want  to go and see what you want to see but I  like the strides Microsoft is made here  not only does the update give the Xbox  one a facelift it feels like the  dashboard is snappier and more  responsive this update is expected to  roll out to everyone in February so be  on the lookout for these features very  soon  you
 

